---
import Layout from 'src/layouts/Layout.astro';
import GitHub from 'src/components/GitHub.astro';

import PDF from 'src/components/PDF.astro';
import ImageGrid from 'src/components/ImageGrid.astro';
---

<Layout page="Year 3">
	<div class="project">
		<h3>Games Preproduction/IP3: Puffy MacPuffer</h3>
		<GitHub author="dylanusinggithub" repo="Puffy-McPuffer" extra="https://kokwithoutak.github.io"></GitHub>

		<a href="/Year3/PuffyTitle.png"><img src="/Year3/PuffyTitle.png" style="float: left;"/></a>

		<p>
			The real hightlight of this year. <a href="https://www.scottishopera.org.uk/pop-up-opera-2025/">Puffy MacPuffer</a> is an opera about the titular 
			character Puffy a puffer boat and their adventure through the five Crabbit Canals. We initally started with only a team of six: three programmers, 
			one artist and two designers, though one had to unfortunetly leave after the first week. We met with out client, Ian Piercy, once every few weeks
			for brain storming.
		</p>

		<p>
			The first half of the year was spent in preproduction, the first few weeks was comming up with ideas and looking at the <a href="https://gcugames.itch.io/puffy-mcpuffers-grand-canal-adventure">
			previous year's attempt</a>, we came up with with 3 ideas:
		</p>

		<div id="PuffyPitch">
			<ImageGrid location="Year3" images={[`IP3Concept1.png`, `IP3Concept2.png`, `IP3Concept3.png`]} link="PitchSlides.pdf"></ImageGrid>
		</div>

		<a href="/Year3/IP3GyroTest.png"><img src="/Year3/IP3GyroTest.png" style="float: right; height:300px; width:150px"/></a>
		<p>
			Concept 1 was a point and click 2D scroller where you interact with the canals and they would give you objectives that would allow you to progress with some extra
			goodies to ogle at when clicking on them.

			Concept 2 was a variation of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pipe_Mania">Pipe Mania</a> where you're placing down sections of canals to guide Puffy around,
			and they would win by going through X amount of pieces. Sometimes the board would have pre-placed titles to help or hinder the player, some levels would have a 
			special mode making the player need to go through all the in addition to the usual requirement. And an alterntive mode for the board to be completely filled and
			a path is created by rotating the pieces.

			Concept 3 was a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Snap">Pokémon Snap</a>-esque game where you're on the clyde canal and are taking photos of the
			landmarks, whenever you did this infomation would appear about that landmark, you would be scored on how well it was taken and if the object was intresting. All the photos
			taken could then be viewed in a gallery. This game was to be more of a learning experiance similar to the original show itself.
		</p>

		<p>
			For the Pokémon Snap idea I was so excited for it I went ahead and try and make a demo of the gyro controls we wanted. This was done by building an android app to then test,
			though the idea was this was to end up being played on iPads due to - at the time - the increased usage of them in educational spaces. Sadly due to issues with gyrolock
			and the more fundamental issue of it not working on WebGL (our target platform).
		</p>	

		<p>
			Concept 2 and 3 were our favourties, especially concept 3 though we were apprehensive about concept 3's due to only having the one artist and only having a few months
			to create it all, and the Lectures and client agreed so we went with concept 2 but were told to expand it.
		</p>

		<p>

		</p>
	</div>  
</Layout>
